# ==============================================================================
# File:    dashboard.service.x11  (one of two variants; install.sh picks)
# Purpose: US-399 carousel dashboard kiosk, X11 session. Chromium kiosk that
#          renders the carousel + polls the localhost state server. Touch
#          enabled (A-5: --touch-events=enabled). Loads /dashboard.html
#          same-origin so the token is injected (token SSOT).
# Author:  Ralph Agent (Rex)
# Created: 2026-06-30 -- Sprint 49 US-399 (carousel shell)
#
# A-1 hand-off: NOT WantedBy=graphical.target -- started by the splash-boot
#   `OnSuccess=eclipse-dashboard.service` directive only after HEALTHY_YIELD.
#   No [Install] section by design (dependency-started, not enabled).
#
# Token SSOT + assets: requires eclipse-states-http with /opt/dashboard on its
#   --assets-dir search path (deploy/eclipse-states-http.service, US-399 A-2).
#
# Type=simple [A-8]. __PI_USER__ substituted by install.sh at install time.
#
# US-522 (F-124) -- `--disable-gpu`: the bench UI froze because chromium's GPU
#   command-buffer context died and then HOT-LOOPED on the fatal
#   `AllocateRingBuffer()` failure (6M errors in one boot, renderer + GPU process
#   CPU-pegged, no crash, display stale while X stayed live). Root: the Pi 5 v3d
#   GPU on a 64 MiB CMA pool driving the animated carousel with GPU rasterization
#   ON. Atlas RCA:
#   offices/architect/findings/2026-08-02-pi-ui-freeze-chromium-gpu-command-buffer-hotloop.md
#
#   THE FLAG IS AN OVERRIDE, NOT A DELETION. `--enable-gpu-rasterization` is not
#   in this repo -- Debian/RPi-OS exports it from /etc/chromium.d/default-flags,
#   which the /usr/bin/chromium WRAPPER sources. The wrapper then runs
#   `exec $LIBDIR/$APPNAME $CHROMIUM_FLAGS "$@"` (/usr/bin/chromium:195), so the
#   OS flags land FIRST and this ExecStart's argv lands LAST. Verified live on
#   the Pi rather than assumed -- the composed cmdline read
#   `... --enable-gpu-rasterization ... --use-angle=gles --disable-gpu <url>`.
#
#   WHY `--disable-gpu` AND NOT `--disable-gpu-rasterization`: the failure is in
#   the GPU COMMAND BUFFER, which compositing uses as well as raster -- so
#   turning raster off alone reduces the pressure without removing the
#   mechanism. `--disable-gpu` takes hardware GL/v3d out of the path entirely,
#   and it has NO counterpart in the injected set, so nothing in /etc/chromium.d
#   can contradict it and the fix does not depend on flag ORDER. This is a 2D
#   card UI on a 480x320 panel; the Pi 5 CPU renders it without difficulty. A
#   live probe on this Pi ran the composed flag set against the real dashboard
#   URL on :0 for 12s: chromium stayed up, 0 AllocateRingBuffer, no GL init
#   failure. (A software-GL gpu-process may still be present -- the claim is
#   that the v3d/CMA exhaustion mechanism is gone, not that no GPU process runs.)
#
# US-522 (reopen 2026-08-03) -- `--password-store=basic`: a repeating
#   "Authentication Required" keyring dialog was painting OVER the kiosk. With no
#   `--password-store`, chromium auto-detects a Linux backend and picks the GNOME
#   keyring for its OSCrypt "Safe Storage" key. This Pi's Default keyring is
#   password-protected (~/.local/share/keyrings/Default_Keyring.keyring, 0600) and
#   under PASSWORDLESS auto-login pam_gnome_keyring never unlocks it -- so the
#   collection stays LOCKED, chromium's unlock request reaches gcr-prompter, and
#   the dialog appears. `basic` keeps the safe-storage key in chromium's own
#   profile instead. No meaningful security downgrade: that profile is the wiped
#   /tmp/dashboard-chromium below and this kiosk stores no real password.
#
#   Atlas live-tested it on the Pi; grounded again from the journal, which is also
#   what shows the fix belongs HERE and not on the splash unit: gcr-prompter
#   PerformPrompt fired Aug 03 05:43:09 / 08:33:52 / 08:52:23 -- recurring, and
#   every one ~9h AFTER splash-boot exited (Aug 02 20:20:21), with none in the
#   splash's own 9.8s window. The prompts track the LONG-RUNNING dashboard
#   chromium. Once applied, the effect is visible as
#   `key_storage_linux.cc: Selected backend for OSCrypt: BASIC_TEXT`.
#
#   NOTE the live box's unit was hand-patched and ALSO carried
#   `--enable-logging=stderr --remote-debugging-port=9222`. Those were test aids
#   and are deliberately NOT adopted here -- an open DevTools port on a
#   car-mounted kiosk is unauthenticated full-page control. A test fences it.
# ==============================================================================

[Unit]
Description=Eclipse OBD carousel dashboard kiosk (X11)
After=graphical.target eclipse-states-http.service
Wants=eclipse-states-http.service

[Service]
Type=simple
User=__PI_USER__
Environment=DISPLAY=:0
ExecStart=__CHROMIUM_BIN__ \
  --kiosk \
  --touch-events=enabled \
  --noerrdialogs --disable-infobars --hide-scrollbars \
  --autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required \
  --check-for-update-interval=31536000 \
  --password-store=basic \
  --user-data-dir=/tmp/dashboard-chromium \
  --enable-logging=stderr --log-level=0 \
  http://127.0.0.1:9899/dashboard.html
Restart=on-failure
RestartSec=2
